    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **64 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 including the four tests that encode this change (Cp28, Cp52, Cp35, Cp10) and every existing duplicate/household test.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 redesigned the identity key:\n- `getIdentityKey()` now returns the lower-case 64-char hex **SHA-256** over `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName)` (email lower-cased, null\u2192empty).\n- Added a self-contained `sha256Hex(...)` helper and a public static `soundex(...)` (standard American Soundex: first letter + 3 digits, `h`/`w` transparent, vowels reset the run) plus its `soundexDigit(...)` mapping. I implemented Soundex directly rather than adding `commons-codec`, since that library isn't on the classpath and the build is offline.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 duplicate detection is now the single identity key:\n- Removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block (the one that rejected a second owner sharing `householdId` without email/`sharesHousehold`). `householdId`/`householdSize` are still computed and still drive household sizing and the level ceiling.\n- Rewrote the soft-match to trigger when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match (flagging the earliest such owner), instead of the old telephone-difference check.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` schema description and example to the new SHA-256/soundex form.\n\nNet behavioral effect, matching the spec: two owners with the same last name + postcode but different telephones are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they're created as a soft match, while a full identity repeat (same telephone + email + last-name soundex) still collides with 409, ignoring deleted owners and applying the email-domain blocklist first.",
